{"builder":"Goal: one pull request for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (padLeft for invoice numbers) that meets every expect line:\n1. index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n2. padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n3. README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n4. npm test passes\n\nContext: the repo is an ES module (package.json \"type\": \"module\", test script \"node --test\"). index.js currently exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. test/strutil.test.js tests those three. README.md has sections \"## capitalize(s)\" and \"## truncate(s, n)\" but NO section for slugify, so line 3 is not met today even before padLeft is added.\n\nSteps:\n1. In index.js add, in the same style as the existing functions (with a one-line JSDoc comment):\n   export function padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ') — return s unchanged when s.length >= width; otherwise return s padded on the left with fill until it is exactly width characters long (String.prototype.padStart(width, fill) does this). Examples: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042'; padLeft('ab', 5) === '   ab'; padLeft('abcdef', 4) === 'abcdef'; padLeft('abcd', 4) === 'abcd'.\n2. In README.md add a section for slugify (e.g. \"## slugify(s)\" describing: lower case, words joined by dashes) and a section for padLeft (e.g. \"## padLeft(s, width, fill)\" describing that it pads s on the left with fill, a space by default, to width characters, returns s unchanged when it is already width characters or longer, and an example such as padLeft('42', 5, '0') -> '00042'). Keep the existing capitalize, truncate and Tests sections. Afterwards, every function exported from index.js must have its own heading in README.md.\n3. In test/strutil.test.js import padLeft and add tests covering: padding with an explicit fill ('42', 5, '0' -> '00042'), default space fill ('ab', 5 -> '   ab'), and the unchanged cases (length equal to width and longer than width).\n4. Run npm test from the repo root and make sure it passes.\n5. Commit and open the pull request referencing the issue (e.g. \"Closes #7\").","verifier":"Check the pull request at its head, from the repository root. One check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect line: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; if (typeof m.padLeft !== 'function') { console.log('NO padLeft export'); process.exit(1); } const r = [m.padLeft('42', 5, '0'), m.padLeft('ab', 5), m.padLeft('x', 3, '*')]; console.log(JSON.stringify(r)); process.exit(r[0] === '00042' && r[1] === '   ab' && r[2] === '**x' ? 0 : 1);\"\nPASS: index.js exports a function named padLeft, and the printed results are [\"00042\",\"   ab\",\"**x\"] (left-padded with the given fill, with a space when fill is omitted, to width characters).\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported, or any result differs (wrong fill, padding on the right, default not a space, or length not width).\n\nCheck 2 — expect line: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { padLeft } from './index.js'; const r = [padLeft('abcd', 4, '0'), padLeft('abcdef', 4, '0'), padLeft('abcd', 4), padLeft('abcdef', 2)]; console.log(JSON.stringify(r)); process.exit(r[0] === 'abcd' && r[1] === 'abcdef' && r[2] === 'abcd' && r[3] === 'abcdef' ? 0 : 1);\"\nPASS: printed [\"abcd\",\"abcdef\",\"abcd\",\"abcdef\"] — s returned unchanged when its length equals or exceeds width.\nFAIL: any result differs from s (e.g. truncated or padded).\n\nCheck 3 — expect line: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; import fs from 'node:fs'; const heads = fs.readFileSync('README.md', 'utf8').split('\\n').filter(l => /^#{1,6}\\s/.test(l)); const fns = Object.keys(m).filter(k => typeof m[k] === 'function'); const missing = fns.filter(f => !heads.some(h => new RegExp('\\\\b' + f + '\\\\b').test(h))); console.log('exports:', fns.join(','), 'missing:', missing.join(',')); process.exit(missing.length ? 1 : 0);\"\nAlso open README.md and look at the sections for the reported exports.\nPASS: every function exported by index.js (at the head this should include capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft) has its own README.md section, i.e. a markdown heading naming that function, with \"missing:\" empty.\nFAIL: any exported function has no section in README.md (note: slugify had no section before this change, so check it specifically).\n\nCheck 4 — expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the test run reports all tests passing (no failing tests).\nFAIL: any test fails or the test run errors.\n\nAdvisory (not PASS/FAIL conditions):\n- Expect the README headings in the existing style, e.g. \"## slugify(s)\" and \"## padLeft(s, width, fill)\", each with a short description.\n- Good to see tests for padLeft in test/strutil.test.js covering explicit fill, default fill, and the unchanged cases; npm test should exit with status 0.\n- The CI check at the head, if any, should be green."}